  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "Prior to the first occupation of the use hereby permitted, full details of the materials, height, finish, and color of the proposed boundary treatments to the flank and rear of the property shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved boundary treatments shall be installed in accordance with the approved details prior to the first use of the facility and maintained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To secure visual privacy and safeguard the residential amenities of adjoining occupiers in accordance with Sutton Local Plan Policies 28 and 29.",
    "Prior to the commencement of development, details of proposed renewable energy technologies, including roof plans, product specifications, generating capacity and calculations to demonstrate that the proposed renewable energy technology will achieve at least a 10% reduction in overall carbon dioxide emissions (regulated plus non-regulated) must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing. \r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The premises shall be operated at all times in strict accordance with the provisions, shift patterns, visitor restrictions, and staff handover protocols set out in the approved Operational Management Plan.\r\rReason: To protect the residential amenity of neighboring occupiers and prevent late-night noise and disturbance in accordance with Sutton Local Plan Policy 29."
  ],
